  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## Setlist highlights\n\n- **Friends Again**: rare: 5 archived performances [6]\n- **Where To Begin**: back after 21 archived shows (615 days) [6]\n- **Carnival Time**: rare: 7 archived performances [6]\n- **Move On Up**: rare: 10 archived performances [6]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **mmj2010-04-23.mk22-mk4v.flac16** (recommended): source not stated; 20 songs; 115 min; rated 5/5 by 2 [1]\n- **mmj2010-04-23.dpasax**: source not stated; 20 songs; 115 min [3]\n- **mmj2010-04-23.mk22-mk4v.flac24**: source not stated; 20 songs; 115 min [2]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- Reviewer attended with father, a Preservation Hall fan, who later suffered a stroke [5]\n- Preservation Hall Jazz Band joined the band for the final four songs [1]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **mmj2010-04-23.mk22-mk4v.flac16**: taped by Taylor Caine; transferred by taylorc; source: [16bit] Schoeps mk22> KCY> Sonosax SX-M2/LS + Schoeps mk4v> KC5> M222> NT222> Lunatec V3> SD 744t (@24bit/96kHz) [1]. Also: Jason Lonchar provided the tubes and V3 microphone for the recording [1]\n- **mmj2010-04-23.dpasax**: taped by Brian Hadella; transferred by Brian Hadella; source: DPA 4023 (DFC at FOH, Clamped onto FOH cage, 7' up, DIN) > Sonosax SX-M2 > Edirol R44 (24/48) [3]. Also: Audio was recorded on a Sonosax SX-M2 and Edirol R44 recorder [3]\n- **mmj2010-04-23.mk22-mk4v.flac24**: taped by Taylor Caine; transferred by taylorc; source: [24bit] Schoeps mk22> KCY> Sonosax SX-M2/LS + Schoeps mk4v> KC5> M222> NT222> Lunatec V3> SD 744t (@24bit/96kHz) [2]",
